{
  "title": "Little Leaguer's Shoulder",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3056/little-leaguers-shoulder",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 27 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Little Leaguer's shoulder is an overuse injury occuring in young baseball pitchers resulting in epiphysiolysis of the proximal humerus (a Salter Harris Type 1 injury).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with radiographs of the shoulder showing a widened proximal humerus physis in comparison to contralateral shoulder.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is cessation of throwing, followed by PT and progressive throwing program after sufficient rest.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "seen in **skeletally immature overhead athletes**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "adolescent pitchers",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "10% of all shoulder pain in pediatric patients is related to throwing",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "occasionally seen in tennis players",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**males** > females",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "age 11-16 years",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "repetitive torsional and distractive stresses at the physis (Saltar Harris 1 injury)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pitching",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "phases",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**late cocking**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "shoulder is maximally externally rotated, leading to extreme rotatory torque through the growth plate, approximately 400% greater than the fragile physeal cartilage can tolerate",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**deceleration**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "opposing forces of forward arm motion and rotator cuff results in excessive eccentric physeal stress",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**breaking pitches** are implicated",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**number of pitches is the most important factor**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cell biology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hypertrophic zone of the physis is affected",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "weakest portion of the growth plate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**decreased pitch velocity**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "decreased pitch accuracy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diffuse arm and **shoulder pain with throwing**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "worse in late cocking or deceleration phases",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pain resolves with rest",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**point tenderness over lateral proximal humerus, at the shoulder physis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain reproduced with shoulder rotation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "glenohumeral internal rotation deficit",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "patients with GIRD are three times more likely to experience recurrent symptoms",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommends views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP in external rotation, scapular Y and axillary views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**contralateral shoulder** can obtained for comparison in subtle cases",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**widened proximal humerus physis in comparison to contralateral shoulder**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3056/images/19a_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "metaphyseal bony changes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3056/images/ll%201.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3056/images/ll%202.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may have normal radiographs (17%)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "edema around physis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3056/images/19b_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "may be helpful to rule out other pathology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "labral tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "partial articular-sided rotator cuff tears (less likely)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "cessation of throwing, followed by PT and progressive throwing program after sufficient rest",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "mainstay of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**refrain from pitching for 3 months**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "start progressive throwing program only after symptom resolution",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**physical therapy**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**rotator cuff strengthening**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "posterior shoulder capsule stretching",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "core strengthening",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**progressive throwing program**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "start with short tosses at low velocity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "slowly progress distance and velocity of throws",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Prognosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The large majority of patients will return to pre-injury levels",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prevention",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**proper pitching mechanics**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "using pitching coaches",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**discourage breaking ball pitches**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**until skeletal maturity**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**enforcement of pitch counts**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**as well as days off for shoulder rest**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**avoid year-round pitching**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
